{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5jBWByZAy4p5wWxKtUh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll start implementing the backend ticket. Let me begin with the ANALYSIS phase.\n\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n\n**Requirement, restated**: Add a POST endpoint to confirm shipments, moving CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED status idempotently, while rejecting CANCELLED shipments with 409 and unknown IDs with 404.\n\n**Repository findings**:\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- ShipmentController existing endpoints: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:26-56`\n- Error handling: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:18-24`\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Existing tests: `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`\n\n**Conventions this repository has**:\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404)\n- Error responses have centralized handling via GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Successful POST operations return ResponseEntity with appropriate status (201 for create, 200 for other operations)\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions and check both status and error body shape\n- Repository pattern with in-memory storage (ConcurrentHashMap)\n- Error codes are machine-readable enums in ApiErrorBody\n\n**Affected files**:\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Must add new ErrorCode for SHIPMENT_CANCELLED or similar (e.g., SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add @PostMapping for `/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for the new endpoint covering all four cases\n\n**Risks**:\n- Breaking existing tests if not careful with return types or status codes\n- Introducing new error codes that might conflict with domain semantics\n- Not handling idempotency correctly (must return 200 OK, not error)\n- State mutations being lost if repository isn't updated correctly\n\n**Open questions**:\n- Should the confirm endpoint return 200 OK or 204 No Content? The ticket doesn't specify. Based on the pattern in the controller (create returns 201 with body), and the requirement to \"return the shipment\", I'll use 200 OK with the shipment body.\n- What HTTP status/error code for confirming a CANCELLED shipment? The ticket says \"rejected with HTTP 409\", which maps to ConflictException, but we need an ErrorCode. I'll add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE or similar.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes**:\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add a new ErrorCode `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to represent attempts to confirm shipments in invalid states (CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new method:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   The method will:\n   - Find the shipment by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — create, confirm, verify status is CONFIRMED\n   - `idempotent confirm of confirmed shipment` — create, confirm twice, verify both succeed and status remains CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirm of cancelled shipment` — create, manually set to CANCELLED, confirm, verify 409 with error code\n   - `rejects confirm of unknown shipment` — confirm non-existent, verify 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected**:\n- Adding a separate service layer: Would over-engineer for this simple state transition. Direct repository usage in controller is consistent with other endpoints.\n- Using PUT instead of POST: The ticket specifically asks for POST, which is appropriate for an action endpoint.\n- Adding a ConfirmShipmentRequest DTO: Not needed; shipmentId is in the path and no other data is required.\n\n**Data and error flow**:\n\nFor CREATED → CONFIRMED:\n1. GET shipment from repository by ID\n2. Check if null → throw ResourceNotFoundException → 404\n3. Check if status is CANCELLED → throw ConflictException → 409\n4. If status is CREATED: create new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED, save to repository\n5. If status is CONFIRMED: do nothing\n6. Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) → 200 with body\n\n**Test strategy**:\n1. Test 1: Verify CREATED → CONFIRMED transition persists\n2. Test 2: Verify confirming CONFIRMED again returns 200 and doesn't change status\n3. Test 3: Verify confirming CANCELLED returns 409 with correct error code\n4. Test 4: Verify confirming non-existent returns 404 with correct error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nI'll now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1219,"cache_read_input_tokens":16536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1219},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"969fcd24-fa87-4b9e-9b05-c60a5353853d","uuid":"fd763887-d83f-4708-837d-36d6e832a9fd","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:51:17.742Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5jBViho27mWZvfnWXXJ"}
